  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 203 AM MDT SAT AUG 8 2026\nA gradual cooling trend will set in for the long-term period, as\nthe Great Basin high pressure aloft weakens and shifts towards\nthe Four Corners region. Near zonal flow aloft will keep the\narea dry for the start of the long-term period. Come mid-week \nthis coming week, a deepening trough near the west coast will \nput our area under more southwesterly flow aloft. This will \nallow for mid-level moisture to work its way north again. The \nLREF mean has positive PWAT anomalies reaching the Nevada \nborder come Thursday, continuing to push north through the end \nof the period. This will allow for increasing chances of showers\nand thunderstorms to end the coming work week. At the end of \nthe period, timing becomes uncertain on when the aforementioned \ntrough will come across our area.",
